  "mn141:10.1": "",
  "mn141:10.2": "In passages where the Buddha defines stress, (e.g., <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn56.11'>SN 56:11</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn22'>DN 22</a>), he includes the statements, “association with the unbeloved is stressful; separation from the loved is stressful,” prior to “not getting what one wants is stressful.” For some reason, in passages where Ven. Sāriputta defines stress (here and at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn9'>MN 9</a> and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn28'>MN 28</a>), he drops these statements from the definition.",
